WEBVTT


00:00:03.000 --> 00:00:08.000
Resync from Scream of the
Banshee [2011] -Self Sync to Fit


00:00:10.000 --> 00:00:15.000
by Smurfin. mail@gmail. com


00:05:43.600 --> 00:05:46.301
Santa Mira Archive Project


00:05:46.369 --> 00:05:49.255
Number A2721.


00:05:49.757 --> 00:05:51.073
Marble vase.


00:05:51.708 --> 00:05:53.259
Ming Dynasty.


00:05:53.326 --> 00:05:54.443
Replica.


00:05:54.511 --> 00:05:55.878
Condition, fair.


00:05:55.963 --> 00:05:59.632
Normal wear and tear.
Restoration, complete.


00:07:09.150 --> 00:07:11.017
Fall semester
starts in two weeks.


00:07:11.235 --> 00:07:13.302
Think you'll be done in
time, Professor Whelan?


00:07:14.654 --> 00:07:16.070
We're close.


00:07:16.138 --> 00:07:17.539
We're very close.


00:07:17.607 --> 00:07:18.607
Let me give you a hand.


00:07:18.674 --> 00:07:20.408
Oh, no. I'm fine.


00:07:20.476 --> 00:07:22.043
I thought it'd be a lot
faster to box and store away


00:07:22.111 --> 00:07:23.444
all that old stuff.


00:07:23.513 --> 00:07:24.546
You know history.


00:07:24.614 --> 00:07:26.715
It always needs a
lot of polishing.


00:07:26.782 --> 00:07:28.149
Good night. You
have a good night.


00:07:38.927 --> 00:07:40.945
Santa Mira Archive Project


00:07:41.013 --> 00:07:44.231
Number B47305.


00:07:44.298 --> 00:07:46.667
Indian Head coin circa 1915.


00:07:46.735 --> 00:07:48.185
Condition, good.


00:07:48.253 --> 00:07:50.788
I just found
Mesozoic era fossils


00:07:50.856 --> 00:07:52.005
of an Apatosaurus


00:07:52.040 --> 00:07:55.409
next to a series of
thesis papers on Methuselah


00:07:55.476 --> 00:07:57.662
and we are one step
closer to completion.


00:07:59.931 --> 00:08:01.348
WHELAN: Hey, guys.


00:08:01.416 --> 00:08:03.200
And two major steps back.


00:08:04.968 --> 00:08:06.269
(SIGHS)


00:08:06.337 --> 00:08:07.504
Do they realize how far
behind we actually are?


00:08:09.173 --> 00:08:11.240
I haven't told them yet.


00:08:11.308 --> 00:08:14.711
Well, then let's
show the Dean this.


00:08:14.779 --> 00:08:18.515
Fossilized rat circa 1954.
Very fine year for rats.


00:08:21.668 --> 00:08:22.435
Or


00:08:24.254 --> 00:08:26.205
rusty gauntlet.


00:08:26.274 --> 00:08:28.040
Gauntlet trumps rat.


00:08:29.058 --> 00:08:30.142
Scottish?


00:08:32.162 --> 00:08:35.447
Actually Irish. You can
tell from the design.


00:08:35.514 --> 00:08:37.415
I'm thinking 12th century.


00:08:37.483 --> 00:08:40.118
Yeah. Can I? Just...
Please. Thank you.


00:08:47.393 --> 00:08:48.677
This came with it, too.


00:08:49.829 --> 00:08:51.079
(MIMICKING WHIZZING)


00:08:54.983 --> 00:08:56.167
Oh!


00:08:56.234 --> 00:08:58.035
Great. Section three.


00:09:00.738 --> 00:09:02.706
Section three?


00:09:02.775 --> 00:09:04.408
Do we even have a section three?


00:09:04.476 --> 00:09:05.576
Oh!


00:09:05.644 --> 00:09:08.062
Yeah. Remember it had that
musty old grandma smell.


00:09:09.898 --> 00:09:12.283
Maybe we missed something.


00:09:12.318 --> 00:09:14.235
Maybe we didn't.


00:09:14.303 --> 00:09:16.053
Look, I told my parents


00:09:16.205 --> 00:09:19.023
I'd come home and
visit next week.


00:09:19.090 --> 00:09:20.792
Am I the only one
that hasn't made plans


00:09:20.908 --> 00:09:22.959
once we're finished?


00:09:23.110 --> 00:09:24.461
We finish when we finish.


00:09:34.755 --> 00:09:36.606
You're gonna wear that
thing all day, aren't you?


00:09:38.642 --> 00:09:40.994
Just come on over here.


00:09:41.045 --> 00:09:44.131
Jeez. How do you get used to being
down here in the dark all day?


00:09:47.550 --> 00:09:48.768
How come you're late?


00:09:49.936 --> 00:09:51.037
Sorry.


00:09:55.091 --> 00:09:56.892
Hi, Ms. Whelan.


00:09:59.479 --> 00:10:01.029
Hello, Kurtis.


00:10:04.467 --> 00:10:05.951
You should probably go.


00:10:08.221 --> 00:10:09.988
See you tonight. I'll
pick you up later, okay?


00:10:10.056 --> 00:10:11.090
Okay.


00:10:13.542 --> 00:10:15.410
So, what's the damage?


00:10:16.245 --> 00:10:18.346
You should go with Otto.


00:10:18.413 --> 00:10:20.415
What's section three?


00:10:20.482 --> 00:10:22.634
It's a lovely place. Nice decor.


00:10:22.701 --> 00:10:24.235
Wonderful aroma.


00:10:24.303 --> 00:10:25.970
Right this way.


00:10:32.544 --> 00:10:34.913
Always lift with


00:10:36.114 --> 00:10:38.282
the knees. (GRUNTS)


00:10:38.349 --> 00:10:39.683
Lift about 10 of these a day


00:10:39.750 --> 00:10:40.918
and you will be well on your way


00:10:40.985 --> 00:10:43.420
to the physique
you see before you.


00:10:46.357 --> 00:10:47.991
Okay.


00:10:48.059 --> 00:10:49.092
(EXCLAIMS)


00:10:49.160 --> 00:10:50.460
Find this.


00:10:50.528 --> 00:10:51.895
Let's see.


00:10:53.214 --> 00:10:54.464
A red square?


00:10:54.532 --> 00:10:56.133
Could be anything.


00:10:56.200 --> 00:11:00.503
Could be a fully solved Rubik's
Cube with the red side facing up.


00:11:00.538 --> 00:11:03.507
Could be a single tile
from a checkerboard.


00:11:03.573 --> 00:11:08.494
Could be a metaphor for communism
or it could symbolize guilt.


00:11:09.112 --> 00:11:10.663
I'll keep an open mind.


00:11:55.873 --> 00:11:56.890
Otto!


00:11:59.594 --> 00:12:01.562
The square is another room.


00:12:29.706 --> 00:12:31.040
OTTO: Look out!
(SHAYLA SCREAMING)


00:12:31.108 --> 00:12:32.475
(CRASHING)


00:12:41.835 --> 00:12:43.186
Shayla!


00:12:43.903 --> 00:12:44.986
I'm okay.


00:12:45.054 --> 00:12:46.138
Wet and a little icky,


00:12:46.206 --> 00:12:47.755
but I'm good.


00:12:48.558 --> 00:12:49.658
What the hell happened?


00:12:49.692 --> 00:12:51.610
She found a false wall.


00:12:53.212 --> 00:12:55.147
It's not like I
used a sledgehammer.


00:12:55.215 --> 00:12:58.099
It was already falling apart.


00:12:58.167 --> 00:13:00.202
How am I gonna explain
this to the school?


00:13:01.337 --> 00:13:02.554
There's something back there.


00:13:02.622 --> 00:13:04.055
I thought that's...


00:13:09.194 --> 00:13:10.795
You're welcome.


00:13:14.166 --> 00:13:15.449
Shayla.


00:13:17.051 --> 00:13:18.836
That went well.


00:13:19.905 --> 00:13:21.355
I need more light.


00:13:30.348 --> 00:13:31.365
Hi.


00:13:34.152 --> 00:13:36.019
What? It's for protection.


00:13:56.273 --> 00:13:59.292
Well, I think we've found
what we're looking for.


00:14:00.026 --> 00:14:02.010
You know what this means?


00:14:02.078 --> 00:14:03.027
Yup.


00:14:03.095 --> 00:14:04.529
We're dining in tonight.


00:14:04.547 --> 00:14:06.081
Burgers or Chinese?


00:14:46.622 --> 00:14:49.307
There's a similarity
in craftsmanship.


00:14:50.908 --> 00:14:53.894
It's the emblem for the
Irish Templar Knights.


00:14:56.264 --> 00:14:57.630
Interesting.


00:15:05.422 --> 00:15:07.040
What do you think is in it?


00:15:07.075 --> 00:15:08.141
Another box?


00:15:11.195 --> 00:15:13.229
There's some condensation.


00:15:18.885 --> 00:15:20.419
It's vibrating.


00:15:23.924 --> 00:15:26.409
I've never heard
anything like it.


00:15:30.380 --> 00:15:31.647
Sounds like it's...


00:15:33.216 --> 00:15:34.350
Sounds like it's breathing.


00:15:35.351 --> 00:15:36.351
(SCOFFS)


00:15:41.857 --> 00:15:42.974
(THUDDING)


00:15:45.177 --> 00:15:47.078
That's not funny.


00:15:49.481 --> 00:15:50.865
Listen to it.


00:15:55.337 --> 00:15:56.804
(HEAVY BREATHING)


00:15:59.859 --> 00:16:01.793
What the hell is that?


00:16:04.330 --> 00:16:05.896
I'm not sure.


00:16:06.614 --> 00:16:08.031
Could be bugs.


00:16:08.099 --> 00:16:10.083
Let's put a moratorium
on the bug talk.


00:16:10.151 --> 00:16:13.053
Done with bugs,
rodents, cardboard boxes


00:16:13.120 --> 00:16:15.755
and any Chinese mystery meat
that attempts to impersonate


00:16:15.823 --> 00:16:17.440
sweet and sour.


00:17:07.506 --> 00:17:08.673
Rolling.


00:17:19.435 --> 00:17:21.536
Santa Mira Archive Project


00:17:21.603 --> 00:17:24.338
Number A2722.


00:17:25.390 --> 00:17:26.807
Condition,


00:17:29.777 --> 00:17:32.913
fair. Needs further restoration.


00:17:34.416 --> 00:17:38.285
We're attempting to open
a metallic Irish box.


00:17:39.621 --> 00:17:41.572
Twelfth century.


00:17:41.640 --> 00:17:45.226
Possibly a relic of
the Templar Knights.


00:17:47.394 --> 00:17:51.331
There's a strange
vibration coming from it.


00:17:51.398 --> 00:17:54.934
We were led to it by a
package containing a gauntlet,


00:17:55.002 --> 00:17:57.403
also from the same time period.


00:17:57.471 --> 00:18:00.423
Number A2723.


00:18:02.609 --> 00:18:04.610
Ready? Roger.


00:18:08.666 --> 00:18:10.083
(GRINDING)


00:18:16.272 --> 00:18:18.006
(PANTING)


00:18:45.717 --> 00:18:49.436
We are looking at an
unexplainable phenomenon.


00:18:51.239 --> 00:18:52.840
It appears to be


00:18:53.942 --> 00:18:56.610
a partially preserved,
severed head.


00:18:57.980 --> 00:19:01.399
Maybe of a deformed person


00:19:04.218 --> 00:19:05.885
or a wild animal.


00:19:08.672 --> 00:19:12.892
Perhaps the metal box contained
some sort of preservative


00:19:12.959 --> 00:19:14.560
presently unknown to us.


00:19:17.598 --> 00:19:19.616
(CELL PHONE RINGING)


00:19:19.684 --> 00:19:22.118
Damn it! Perfect timing.


00:19:28.359 --> 00:19:29.593
(EXHALES)


00:19:31.878 --> 00:19:34.963
Hello, Dean Harris. Funny
that you should call.


00:19:39.619 --> 00:19:42.120
Yeah. No, no, no.
I can handle that.


00:19:43.189 --> 00:19:44.289
Okay.


00:19:51.715 --> 00:19:53.732
This is freaky.


00:19:55.550 --> 00:19:57.301
What do you think?


00:20:01.122 --> 00:20:02.756
I don't know.


00:20:06.978 --> 00:20:08.997
There doesn't seem to
be any decomposition.


00:20:11.450 --> 00:20:12.533
(BOTH GASP)


00:20:18.174 --> 00:20:19.356
(SCREAMING)


00:21:11.457 --> 00:21:13.257
What the hell happened?


00:21:15.861 --> 00:21:17.545
Where's the head?


00:21:17.613 --> 00:21:20.265
(STAMMERS) It just exploded.


00:21:22.301 --> 00:21:23.935
Did you get it?


00:21:25.020 --> 00:21:26.654
(GRUNTING)


00:21:29.624 --> 00:21:30.925
Ah, damn.


00:21:45.257 --> 00:21:47.674
There doesn't seem to
be any decomposition.


00:21:51.829 --> 00:21:53.797
I swear it opened its mouth.


00:21:58.936 --> 00:22:01.037
There's no return address.


00:22:01.105 --> 00:22:03.907
There's no way the
school sent this to us.


00:22:05.609 --> 00:22:07.309
Well, there's gotta be
a plausible explanation.


00:22:07.444 --> 00:22:08.961
Yeah, well, I think we
ruled out the plausible


00:22:09.028 --> 00:22:11.364
the minute we opened the box.


00:22:13.217 --> 00:22:14.967
Maybe we should tell
someone at the school.


00:22:15.035 --> 00:22:16.418
Tell them what happened.


00:22:16.487 --> 00:22:17.986
Tell them what, exactly?


00:22:18.054 --> 00:22:19.555
Yeah, they are gonna look
at the mess in this classroom


00:22:19.623 --> 00:22:21.858
and listen to our
crazy story and say,


00:22:21.925 --> 00:22:23.660
"We hired a bunch
of crack whores.


00:22:25.946 --> 00:22:28.331
"Round up those crack
whores. Take them to prison. "


00:22:28.397 --> 00:22:30.715
Because I'd believe that
a meth lab exploded in here


00:22:30.783 --> 00:22:34.085
before I'd believe a story about
an 800-year-old screaming head


00:22:34.152 --> 00:22:35.820
we found in a box.


00:22:37.906 --> 00:22:40.342
We gotta keep this under
wraps until we figure it out.


00:22:48.718 --> 00:22:50.102
(GROANING)


00:22:55.574 --> 00:22:56.574
(BANSHEE GROWLS)


00:23:22.383 --> 00:23:23.699
(BANSHEE SCREAMING)


00:23:25.252 --> 00:23:26.452
(SCREAMING)


00:23:57.349 --> 00:23:58.550
Shayla?


00:24:57.057 --> 00:24:58.591
(CELL PHONE RINGING)


00:25:09.185 --> 00:25:10.719
Who was it?


00:25:12.472 --> 00:25:13.672
Nobody.


00:26:02.854 --> 00:26:05.872
I've felt, for some
time, disconnected


00:26:05.940 --> 00:26:08.692
from those I once loved.


00:26:08.760 --> 00:26:12.996
My isolation, my
silence, my beliefs,


00:26:14.465 --> 00:26:18.201
were routinely
written off as madness.


00:26:19.269 --> 00:26:23.789
But my madness is
not my affliction.


00:26:27.010 --> 00:26:30.712
Awareness is the curse
that I've been saddled with.


00:26:34.584 --> 00:26:37.236
We didn't find a
key for the casket.


00:26:43.075 --> 00:26:44.959
The apocalypse is coming.


00:26:47.512 --> 00:26:50.147
The Mayans were right.


00:26:50.215 --> 00:26:54.486
The harbinger of death is
coming and will show no mercy.


00:26:55.304 --> 00:26:59.373
Are you listening?


00:27:00.760 --> 00:27:02.677
(VIDEO GAME PLAYING)


00:27:29.270 --> 00:27:30.837
(HIGH-PITCHED BEEPING)


00:27:30.905 --> 00:27:32.105
Ow.


00:27:33.156 --> 00:27:34.490
(GROANS)


00:27:34.558 --> 00:27:35.408
(LAUGHING)


00:27:35.826 --> 00:27:36.793
Ah, crap.


00:27:38.478 --> 00:27:42.265
You cheat, Idaho Commando.
No blades, only guns.


00:27:42.332 --> 00:27:44.333
I will destroy you next time.


00:27:44.401 --> 00:27:46.519
(HIGH-PITCHED BEEPING)


00:27:46.587 --> 00:27:47.637
(GROANING)


00:27:53.994 --> 00:27:55.194
(GROANING)


00:28:10.559 --> 00:28:11.760
(WATER DRIPPING)


00:28:16.365 --> 00:28:17.532
(WINDOW SLAMMING)


00:29:15.972 --> 00:29:17.406
(VOICE GIGGLING)


00:29:37.193 --> 00:29:38.243
(GLASS SHATTERING)


00:30:13.661 --> 00:30:14.778
(GASPS)


00:30:17.532 --> 00:30:18.448
(SCREAMING)


00:30:36.382 --> 00:30:37.399
(GASPS)


00:30:43.206 --> 00:30:44.823
(PANTING)


00:31:01.507 --> 00:31:03.074
(KETTLE WHISTLING)


00:31:19.641 --> 00:31:20.708
SHAYLA: Hey.


00:31:21.509 --> 00:31:22.776
Hey.


00:31:22.843 --> 00:31:24.127
You know, I'm a little too old


00:31:24.194 --> 00:31:27.447
to have a babysitter
waiting up for me.


00:31:27.515 --> 00:31:31.251
No one's waiting up for you.
I just... I couldn't sleep.


00:31:32.437 --> 00:31:34.087
You should go to bed.


00:31:34.155 --> 00:31:35.322
Are you okay?


00:31:38.193 --> 00:31:39.893
Yeah. I'm fine.


00:31:41.278 --> 00:31:42.596
Fine.


00:31:50.470 --> 00:31:51.620
Look.


00:31:53.223 --> 00:31:55.357
I'm sorry about the wall today.


00:31:55.842 --> 00:31:57.260
It's okay.


00:31:58.362 --> 00:32:00.228
Why don't you go to bed?


00:32:00.296 --> 00:32:01.831
I mean, you've gotta get sleep.


00:32:01.898 --> 00:32:03.349
You haven't even started
packing your room yet.


00:32:04.301 --> 00:32:06.218
What was behind it anyway?


00:32:08.238 --> 00:32:09.555
Nothing.


00:32:13.074 --> 00:32:15.075
Why don't you ever
tell me anything?


00:32:16.611 --> 00:32:17.896
I don't wanna fight.


00:32:17.964 --> 00:32:19.464
Yes, you do.


00:32:19.532 --> 00:32:21.282
All the time, actually.


00:32:21.350 --> 00:32:23.151
I can see it in the
way you look at me.


00:32:24.320 --> 00:32:27.071
Why am I such a
disappointment to you?


00:32:27.139 --> 00:32:28.289
Shayla, please.


00:32:28.357 --> 00:32:30.558
I don't wanna do this right now.


00:32:30.626 --> 00:32:33.861
You treat me like a child.
You hate my boyfriend.


00:32:33.929 --> 00:32:36.981
You refuse to even have a
simple conversation with him.


00:32:37.048 --> 00:32:39.733
And, you know, sometimes,
I think you hate me, too,


00:32:39.768 --> 00:32:42.419
because I'm the only
thing you have left of Dad!


00:32:42.554 --> 00:32:45.639
Shayla, I don't wanna
get into this tonight.


00:32:47.324 --> 00:32:50.527
When are you going
to stop blaming me?


00:32:50.595 --> 00:32:54.464
It's not my fault you
weren't around when Dad died.


00:34:07.586 --> 00:34:09.653
(SOBBING)


00:34:56.082 --> 00:34:57.365
Bad night?


00:34:58.284 --> 00:34:59.518
You, too?


00:35:01.587 --> 00:35:03.922
It's not surprising,
considering.


00:35:06.592 --> 00:35:07.626
No.


00:35:08.394 --> 00:35:11.595
It was more than that.


00:35:11.663 --> 00:35:14.965
I kept hearing voices
outside of my place all night.


00:35:16.635 --> 00:35:17.902
Giggling.


00:35:19.038 --> 00:35:20.438
Scratching.


00:35:21.873 --> 00:35:23.841
And it wasn't the storm.


00:35:26.545 --> 00:35:28.779
Something was trying to get in.


00:35:29.881 --> 00:35:31.615
It was taunting me.


00:35:36.187 --> 00:35:37.654
I kept trying to convince myself


00:35:37.721 --> 00:35:40.790
that it was my imagination
getting the best of me.


00:35:47.365 --> 00:35:50.567
Do you want to see what my
imagination did to me last night?


00:36:00.877 --> 00:36:02.044
Yikes.


00:36:07.417 --> 00:36:10.686
Then I guess it's a good
thing I didn't go outside.


00:36:16.810 --> 00:36:17.793
(DOOR OPENING)


00:36:21.731 --> 00:36:23.732
Hey, guys. What's going on?


00:36:25.066 --> 00:36:26.234
Anything weird happened to you


00:36:26.301 --> 00:36:29.187
when you got home last night?


00:36:29.254 --> 00:36:33.825
Well, I was gutted to death
in my Commie Commando game


00:36:33.892 --> 00:36:38.879
which is terribly strange, because
the only weapons available are guns.


00:36:38.947 --> 00:36:43.234
My ear is still ringing and
feeling scabby after last night.


00:36:43.301 --> 00:36:44.818
Mmm.


00:36:44.886 --> 00:36:47.322
Oh, there was a dead
weasel on my front doorstep.


00:36:47.389 --> 00:36:49.073
Otherwise, feeling dandy.


00:36:49.140 --> 00:36:50.141
Oh, my God.


00:36:51.976 --> 00:36:53.059
(EXCLAIMS)


00:37:02.303 --> 00:37:04.505
Professor, what is going on?


00:37:06.974 --> 00:37:10.844
I looked up Broderick
Duncan's name last night.


00:37:10.911 --> 00:37:15.014
He used to teach here.
Retired 10 years ago.


00:37:15.082 --> 00:37:18.851
Then I found all
these creepy videos.


00:37:18.918 --> 00:37:21.487
I know he's gotta have
something to do with this.


00:37:25.225 --> 00:37:28.327
"I am not a god. I am not a man.


00:37:29.279 --> 00:37:31.664
"I am the bringer of darkness.


00:37:31.732 --> 00:37:34.367
"The great wielder of the truth.


00:37:36.603 --> 00:37:40.839
"Mankind has long suffered
at the hands of mortals,


00:37:40.906 --> 00:37:44.709
"but I am the vessel for
which mankind will bow


00:37:44.776 --> 00:37:48.179
"for its forgiveness and
pay for its ultimate sin,


00:37:49.982 --> 00:37:51.249
"complacency. "


00:37:54.987 --> 00:37:56.338
On the one hand,


00:37:56.405 --> 00:37:59.224
he's an esteemed professor
who retired with dignity,


00:37:59.291 --> 00:38:02.961
and on the other hand, he's
an end-of-days prophet of doom.


00:38:03.029 --> 00:38:06.097
Sounds like psycho whackjob is
a more appropriate description.


00:38:07.331 --> 00:38:09.233
Wait. Did you see that?


00:38:13.071 --> 00:38:15.154
Look familiar?


00:38:15.189 --> 00:38:16.906
WHELAN: The Templar seal.


00:38:24.732 --> 00:38:26.467
He's wearing my gauntlet.


00:38:26.534 --> 00:38:27.935
(MOUTHING) My?
That's our connection.


00:38:30.304 --> 00:38:32.305
He has to have been the
one who sent us the gauntlet


00:38:32.372 --> 00:38:34.306
and that led us
directly to the box.


00:38:34.391 --> 00:38:35.641
What a prick.


00:38:35.709 --> 00:38:38.044
We have to find
Broderick Duncan.


00:38:39.379 --> 00:38:42.348
Janie, where are the
employee files kept?


00:38:42.415 --> 00:38:43.382
Section three.


00:38:43.951 --> 00:38:44.951
Not again!


00:38:46.419 --> 00:38:47.520
(SIGHS)


00:38:54.694 --> 00:38:57.096
I really hate the
smell down here.


00:39:22.437 --> 00:39:23.720
WHELAN: Hmm.


00:39:23.788 --> 00:39:26.640
I knew something
didn't sound right.


00:39:26.675 --> 00:39:29.493
Assault charges.
Erratic behavior.


00:39:30.362 --> 00:39:32.062
They offered him a deal.


00:39:32.130 --> 00:39:35.048
Retire gracefully
and never come back.


00:39:36.718 --> 00:39:38.953
Doesn't have a current address.


00:39:42.323 --> 00:39:46.209
But he does have an
assistant. Dr. Frederick Page.


00:39:48.612 --> 00:39:50.429
He was the one
who got him fired.


00:39:58.906 --> 00:40:01.457
JANIE: This guy was heavy
into environmental causes.


00:40:02.309 --> 00:40:04.344
Left shortly after Duncan.


00:40:07.381 --> 00:40:09.316
Maybe he knows where he lives.


00:40:11.335 --> 00:40:12.635
Let's go.


00:40:22.328 --> 00:40:23.529
I'm right behind you.


00:40:23.596 --> 00:40:24.729
OTTO: All right.


00:40:45.100 --> 00:40:46.500
(THUMPING)


00:41:03.018 --> 00:41:04.452
(SCREECHING)


00:41:13.694 --> 00:41:14.794
(EXCLAIMS)


00:41:14.862 --> 00:41:15.811
Pete.


00:41:23.537 --> 00:41:25.188
Pete! Pete!


00:41:42.005 --> 00:41:43.439
(ROARS)


00:41:47.610 --> 00:41:48.944
(SCREAMING)


00:41:56.318 --> 00:41:58.286
Otto! Otto!


00:42:05.511 --> 00:42:07.995
(SCREAMING)


00:42:12.784 --> 00:42:13.985
Whoa, whoa, whoa!


00:42:14.987 --> 00:42:16.721
What's going on?


00:42:18.690 --> 00:42:20.358
You didn't see it?


00:42:20.424 --> 00:42:22.943
We didn't see anything. We
just heard you screaming.


00:42:23.561 --> 00:42:24.978
Are you all right?


00:42:30.501 --> 00:42:31.902
Clearly not.


00:42:33.438 --> 00:42:34.637
(SIRENS WAILING)


00:42:58.479 --> 00:43:00.946
The police say it
was a heart attack.


00:43:02.782 --> 00:43:04.784
What do you think it is?


00:43:09.640 --> 00:43:11.107
I think something
else is going on.


00:43:12.057 --> 00:43:13.692
We looked everywhere.


00:43:13.759 --> 00:43:15.360
Nothing else was
down there with you.


00:43:17.479 --> 00:43:19.380
What are you not telling us?


00:43:23.268 --> 00:43:26.571
In the '60s, the government
tested hallucinogenic weapons.


00:43:26.639 --> 00:43:29.423
LSD was a by-product.


00:43:29.458 --> 00:43:32.477
Maybe something like that was
released when the box was opened.


00:43:34.896 --> 00:43:38.232
You're thinking we're experiencing
some sort of mass psychosis?


00:43:38.299 --> 00:43:42.135
Sioux wasn't even in the room when
that thing evaporated into the air.


00:43:42.203 --> 00:43:44.471
How do you explain
what happened to him?


00:43:47.158 --> 00:43:48.992
Did you find
anything out on Page?


00:43:49.144 --> 00:43:52.563
I got an address. He lives in
that new, downtown Eco-complex.


00:43:54.015 --> 00:43:56.617
Okay. I think I'll
pay him a visit.


00:43:56.684 --> 00:43:59.186
Can I borrow the phone,
the one with the recording?


00:43:59.254 --> 00:44:01.021
Yeah. Here.


00:44:02.706 --> 00:44:04.641
Just keep searching, okay?


00:44:04.708 --> 00:44:05.742
Okay.


00:44:12.482 --> 00:44:14.233
(CELL PHONE RINGING)


00:44:25.395 --> 00:44:28.781
You know, when she's finished
archiving this project,


00:44:29.915 --> 00:44:32.350
we'll be moving.


00:44:32.402 --> 00:44:34.236
She already has the next
gig lined up for next month.


00:44:38.541 --> 00:44:40.007
How long have you
known about this?


00:44:43.112 --> 00:44:44.279
Since we got into town.


00:44:45.915 --> 00:44:47.482
And you're just telling me now?


00:44:47.550 --> 00:44:49.768
I know. I'm sorry. You know...


00:44:51.904 --> 00:44:53.771
I just didn't know
I'd like you this much.


00:44:55.473 --> 00:44:57.324
Okay. Right.


00:45:01.362 --> 00:45:02.546
I was thinking about staying.


00:45:04.483 --> 00:45:06.150
Just thinking?


00:45:09.187 --> 00:45:10.654
She'd never let me.


00:45:10.755 --> 00:45:14.725
I know her. She'd create
some drama to make me go.


00:45:17.761 --> 00:45:20.163
Look, if you do leave,


00:45:22.632 --> 00:45:24.733
maybe I'll go where you go.


00:45:30.374 --> 00:45:31.991
Why should you have
to follow me around?


00:45:34.311 --> 00:45:35.311
You know,


00:45:37.381 --> 00:45:41.150
my dad used to walk me down
to skid row once a month.


00:45:41.218 --> 00:45:44.470
You know, he wanted to show me what life
would be like if I didn't study hard.


00:45:45.521 --> 00:45:46.738
And?


00:45:46.806 --> 00:45:48.707
And...


00:45:48.775 --> 00:45:50.876
And I still got the
lip ring anyway, chica.


00:45:53.028 --> 00:45:55.547
Look, everybody's got their
own reasons for doing things.


00:45:55.614 --> 00:45:58.834
And sometimes they
don't make any sense,


00:45:58.901 --> 00:46:00.769
like your mom, most of the time.


00:46:02.639 --> 00:46:05.023
But if this is how you feel,


00:46:06.743 --> 00:46:10.112
then I'll support
whatever decision you make.


00:46:10.178 --> 00:46:12.579
Good, because I've
already made up my mind.


00:46:13.014 --> 00:46:14.832
Oh.


00:46:14.900 --> 00:46:16.818
Hopefully she'll
listen to me this time.


00:46:19.137 --> 00:46:22.456
What is the only thing you can
break when you say its name?


00:46:24.476 --> 00:46:26.928
I don't feel like I
owe anyone an apology.


00:46:28.313 --> 00:46:30.414
I am not crazy.


00:46:30.482 --> 00:46:32.416
I am not a lunatic.


00:46:32.467 --> 00:46:35.386
I just see the
world for what it is.


00:46:35.453 --> 00:46:38.120
Among our ruins is justice.


00:46:38.188 --> 00:46:40.056
Judgment will be handed down.


00:46:42.226 --> 00:46:43.827
Bean Si.


00:46:43.894 --> 00:46:45.211
Bean Si?


00:46:45.279 --> 00:46:47.480
Is that Spanish for "Yes,
I'd like some beans"?


00:46:52.019 --> 00:46:53.019
Bean Si.


00:46:53.086 --> 00:46:55.254
It's Gaelic for banshee.


00:46:55.322 --> 00:46:57.874
Irish folklore.


00:46:57.941 --> 00:47:00.744
A creature whose scream
warns of imminent death.


00:47:05.181 --> 00:47:06.782
(TYPING)


00:47:12.422 --> 00:47:15.791
Banshees were associated
with five royal Irish families


00:47:15.859 --> 00:47:17.827
up until about the 12th century.


00:47:28.671 --> 00:47:32.089
A banshee can
take on many forms.


00:47:32.157 --> 00:47:36.110
The most common is
that of an old hag.


00:47:36.178 --> 00:47:40.148
But there are also stories of people
encountering a banshee as a waif


00:47:41.116 --> 00:47:42.583
or a seductress.


00:47:54.228 --> 00:47:56.296
And of course,


00:47:56.363 --> 00:47:58.431
if you heard the
banshee's scream,


00:48:00.434 --> 00:48:03.937
it will haunt you until
you accepted death.


00:48:28.879 --> 00:48:30.496
(SCREAMING)


00:48:37.937 --> 00:48:38.937
Otto.


00:48:41.774 --> 00:48:43.074
What? What's wrong?


00:48:44.210 --> 00:48:45.910
So much for the implausible.


00:48:53.152 --> 00:48:56.388
That's pretty much what I saw,
but it had a body this time.


00:48:56.906 --> 00:48:58.189
I didn't see anything.


00:48:59.225 --> 00:49:00.775
Well,


00:49:00.842 --> 00:49:02.577
maybe it didn't want you to.


00:49:04.030 --> 00:49:06.013
I mean, it was
toying with me, it was


00:49:06.081 --> 00:49:08.699
messing with my mind, it
was trying to get me to...


00:49:09.901 --> 00:49:11.518
I don't know, it was
tricking me into...


00:49:11.586 --> 00:49:12.519
Haunting you?


00:49:19.143 --> 00:49:20.143
Silence.


00:49:20.712 --> 00:49:21.745
That's it.


00:49:22.046 --> 00:49:24.064
That's what you
break when you say it.


00:49:24.132 --> 00:49:25.883
That's what Duncan
asked in his clip.


00:49:27.335 --> 00:49:28.768
When I didn't scream,


00:49:29.971 --> 00:49:31.205
that's what saved me.


00:49:31.272 --> 00:49:32.172
It couldn't hurt me.


00:49:34.825 --> 00:49:36.092
You're starting to freak me out.


00:49:37.678 --> 00:49:38.745
Starting?


00:49:47.086 --> 00:49:48.238
Can I help you?


00:49:49.272 --> 00:49:52.208
Uh, yes. My name is
Professor Moira Whelan.


00:49:56.429 --> 00:49:57.964
Ah, you're with the school.


00:49:58.031 --> 00:49:59.981
What can I do for you?


00:50:00.049 --> 00:50:02.751
I only need a moment of your
time. It's about Broderick Duncan.


00:50:04.704 --> 00:50:06.038
A box...


00:50:06.105 --> 00:50:06.955
They're still looking
for that thing?


00:50:07.707 --> 00:50:09.391
No. We found it.


00:50:11.894 --> 00:50:13.128
Well, if that's the case,


00:50:13.195 --> 00:50:15.397
I'm sure you realized
it couldn't be opened.


00:50:15.464 --> 00:50:16.597
It would be a good
idea if you wouldn't...


00:50:16.665 --> 00:50:17.999
Well, you see,
that's the problem.


00:50:18.067 --> 00:50:19.567
We did open it.


00:50:19.635 --> 00:50:20.469
No...


00:50:24.639 --> 00:50:25.639
Come in.


00:50:27.742 --> 00:50:28.859
Hey, guys.


00:50:29.160 --> 00:50:30.611
Where's my mom?


00:50:30.678 --> 00:50:33.397
She went out, but
she'll be back.


00:50:33.465 --> 00:50:35.599
We'll wait. Is there
anything I can do until then?


00:50:36.718 --> 00:50:37.801
You want to help?


00:50:38.603 --> 00:50:39.970
Yeah.


00:50:40.037 --> 00:50:42.205
As always, a little
too late to do that.


00:50:51.131 --> 00:50:52.131
No, thank you.


00:50:59.890 --> 00:51:02.241
Does this look familiar to you?


00:51:02.309 --> 00:51:05.428
I don't recall Duncan or I ever
finding anything quite like that.


00:51:06.029 --> 00:51:07.647
Mmm-hmm.


00:51:07.714 --> 00:51:10.266
Well, it was sent to us


00:51:10.333 --> 00:51:13.019
and it turned out to be the
thing that opened the box.


00:51:13.403 --> 00:51:15.738
Hmm.


00:51:15.805 --> 00:51:18.741
Strange things have been happening
ever since that box was opened.


00:51:20.293 --> 00:51:24.379
Some very wild and
vivid hallucinations.


00:51:24.447 --> 00:51:27.515
Almost like there was some
kind of chemical agent inside.


00:51:28.517 --> 00:51:30.118
Perhaps placed there by Duncan.


00:51:31.154 --> 00:51:33.055
My dear Professor.


00:51:33.122 --> 00:51:35.357
Broderick Duncan is
a very intelligent man


00:51:35.425 --> 00:51:38.526
whose imagination was
his own worst enemy.


00:51:38.593 --> 00:51:43.581
The Templar Box was just one in
a long line of his many crusades.


00:51:43.649 --> 00:51:46.116
I'm not interested in
any crusade, but this one.


00:51:47.219 --> 00:51:48.319
Where can I find Duncan?


00:51:50.222 --> 00:51:52.489
I've left that part
of my life behind me.


00:51:52.557 --> 00:51:56.960
I didn't like who I became
when I was around him.


00:51:57.028 --> 00:51:59.614
But I need you to tell
me everything you know.


00:52:03.518 --> 00:52:04.518
Please.


00:52:11.275 --> 00:52:12.275
What's wrong?


00:52:13.511 --> 00:52:14.961
I'm just worried about you.


00:52:15.028 --> 00:52:16.413
Us.


00:52:16.481 --> 00:52:17.481
And that thing.


00:52:18.383 --> 00:52:19.383
It.


00:52:19.984 --> 00:52:21.018
And?


00:52:21.085 --> 00:52:23.153
And Sioux is dead


00:52:23.221 --> 00:52:25.355
and we both know it
wasn't a heart attack.


00:52:26.590 --> 00:52:30.593
I just... I'm freaked
out, I'm pretty...


00:52:31.328 --> 00:52:32.328
Pretty scared.


00:52:35.399 --> 00:52:36.899
Maybe...


00:52:36.966 --> 00:52:39.468
Maybe we should stick
together tonight.


00:52:39.536 --> 00:52:41.303
Just in case.


00:52:42.605 --> 00:52:44.089
Otto. Yeah.


00:52:45.775 --> 00:52:47.509
Do you realize how
pathetic you sound?


00:52:49.261 --> 00:52:50.729
Yeah. Very.


00:52:55.283 --> 00:52:57.619
And somehow it's the very reason


00:52:59.104 --> 00:53:01.923
I find myself attracted to you.


00:53:13.768 --> 00:53:16.870
And, so you don't
want me to come in...


00:53:16.938 --> 00:53:19.274
No, no, I'm okay.


00:53:19.341 --> 00:53:22.527
Hey, but, maybe next
time, I'll walk you home.


00:53:29.834 --> 00:53:31.318
All right. (MUMBLES)


00:53:57.327 --> 00:53:58.961
(WHIRRING)


00:54:01.582 --> 00:54:04.716
PAGE: Twenty years ago,
we went on an excavation,


00:54:04.784 --> 00:54:06.685
in these wedge caves.


00:54:06.753 --> 00:54:09.321
One in particular
was called Labbacalle


00:54:09.389 --> 00:54:10.790
or Hag's Bed.


00:54:11.991 --> 00:54:13.775
During our dig, we
found a cryptic map


00:54:13.843 --> 00:54:16.894
that was left to us
by early settlers.


00:54:16.962 --> 00:54:21.082
Using the map, we went into
some underground caverns.


00:54:21.150 --> 00:54:24.802
That's where we discovered an
armory buried deep within the walls.


00:54:24.870 --> 00:54:29.090
Artifacts brought to America
from Limerick City in Ireland.


00:54:30.492 --> 00:54:32.260
Then Duncan found that box.


00:54:34.162 --> 00:54:36.781
So he brought it
back to the school?


00:54:38.900 --> 00:54:41.568
He was obsessed with opening it.


00:54:41.636 --> 00:54:43.837
That was one of the things
that led to his dismissal.


00:54:56.785 --> 00:54:59.570
Why didn't he take it with
him? Why bury it in the wall?


00:55:08.796 --> 00:55:09.929
I don't know.


00:55:13.633 --> 00:55:16.185
What did he think he'd
find inside the box?


00:55:19.256 --> 00:55:20.956
He believed it was a weapon.


00:55:22.359 --> 00:55:24.310
And I'd like to know
what he meant by that.


00:55:32.451 --> 00:55:33.785
(GASPS)


00:56:06.901 --> 00:56:07.667
(SCREECHING)


00:56:12.190 --> 00:56:13.608
(CELL PHONE VIBRATING)


00:56:19.664 --> 00:56:20.980
Come on, please, pick up.


00:56:21.048 --> 00:56:22.915
Pick up.


00:56:22.983 --> 00:56:25.901
Hey, this is Otto. Sorry I missed
you. Leave a message. Thanks.


00:56:40.233 --> 00:56:41.417
(SCREECHING)


00:56:41.452 --> 00:56:42.601
(SCREAMING)


00:56:43.520 --> 00:56:44.470
(GROWLING)


00:56:53.446 --> 00:56:55.347
(SCREAMING)


00:57:03.439 --> 00:57:04.906
A head?


00:57:04.974 --> 00:57:06.474
That's what was in this
box the entire time?


00:57:07.476 --> 00:57:09.111
We need to find Duncan


00:57:09.178 --> 00:57:11.345
and then I won't
bother you again.


00:57:15.100 --> 00:57:17.668
Or you can tell me
why your handwriting


00:57:17.736 --> 00:57:19.704
matches the
handwriting on this map.


00:57:23.691 --> 00:57:25.576
When you asked me why Duncan
didn't take the box with him,


00:57:27.011 --> 00:57:28.912
it was me, I was the one
that buried it in the walls.


00:57:29.914 --> 00:57:31.281
To hide it from him!


00:57:32.868 --> 00:57:34.585
Why did you lead us to it?


00:57:35.252 --> 00:57:37.237
Oh, no, no, no, dear.


00:57:37.305 --> 00:57:39.439
I wasn't the one that sent
you the gauntlet or the map.


00:57:40.274 --> 00:57:43.109
That was him. I'm sure of that.


00:57:43.177 --> 00:57:44.811
How did he know where it was?


00:57:47.831 --> 00:57:50.634
He always gets what
he wants from me.


00:57:50.701 --> 00:57:54.237
I tell you, he lost touch
with reality long ago.


00:57:54.305 --> 00:57:56.522
He's a very dangerous man.


00:57:56.590 --> 00:57:57.790
I'll take my chances.


00:57:58.810 --> 00:58:02.211
The Templar Box is
Broderick Duncan's folly.


00:58:02.245 --> 00:58:03.428
When you go chasing windmills,


00:58:03.496 --> 00:58:05.914
all you end up doing is
hurting the ones you love.


00:58:06.883 --> 00:58:07.883
Good day.


00:58:26.802 --> 00:58:28.102
(RATTLING)


00:58:37.212 --> 00:58:39.680
No, no, this is your
mom's classroom...


00:58:42.017 --> 00:58:44.335
WHELAN:... an
unexplainable phenomenon.


00:58:46.038 --> 00:58:47.422
It appears to be...


00:58:56.714 --> 00:58:58.381
(SCRUBBING)


00:59:10.845 --> 00:59:12.278
(RATTLING)


00:59:35.152 --> 00:59:36.369
Come on, Janie, pick up.


00:59:43.709 --> 00:59:44.809
(SCREAMING)


00:59:44.877 --> 00:59:46.727
(BANSHEE SCREAMING)


00:59:53.669 --> 00:59:54.886
(GLASS SHATTERING)


00:59:56.038 --> 00:59:57.338
Janie.


01:00:00.660 --> 01:00:01.726
Kurtis.


01:00:05.581 --> 01:00:06.781
What is your mom involved in?


01:00:08.049 --> 01:00:09.149
I want to go home.


01:00:09.984 --> 01:00:11.351
(WHIRRING)


01:00:57.179 --> 01:00:58.980
Janie. Janie.


01:01:00.766 --> 01:01:01.716
Janie!


01:01:03.569 --> 01:01:04.452
Janie!


01:01:06.255 --> 01:01:07.255
Janie!


01:01:08.591 --> 01:01:09.624
(YELLING) Janie!


01:01:16.249 --> 01:01:17.615
(SIRENS WAILING)


01:01:24.956 --> 01:01:26.023
Something got to her.


01:01:27.359 --> 01:01:30.627
It tried to get to me earlier.


01:01:30.695 --> 01:01:32.729
It's the same thing
that tried to get to you.


01:01:32.797 --> 01:01:33.797
Wasn't it?


01:01:37.635 --> 01:01:39.036
WHELAN: Yes.


01:01:41.139 --> 01:01:42.139
I think...


01:01:44.276 --> 01:01:45.810
I think it might be a banshee.


01:01:48.161 --> 01:01:50.764
Otto... You have
any other theories?


01:01:55.703 --> 01:01:56.870
What did Page say?


01:02:02.025 --> 01:02:03.092
Not much.


01:02:05.580 --> 01:02:06.712
(SIGHS)


01:02:11.535 --> 01:02:12.668
Janie called.


01:02:13.104 --> 01:02:14.353
Before...


01:02:14.420 --> 01:02:16.321
What did she say?


01:02:16.388 --> 01:02:17.939
I don't know.
Where... Where is it?


01:02:21.761 --> 01:02:23.228
JANIE: Come on.


01:02:23.296 --> 01:02:24.612
Come on, pick up. Pick up.


01:02:27.233 --> 01:02:29.034
(JANIE SCREAMING)


01:02:30.720 --> 01:02:32.554
(BANSHEE SCREAMING)


01:02:40.245 --> 01:02:41.879
It didn't kill her
until she screamed.


01:02:46.051 --> 01:02:47.318
Why didn't you pick up?


01:02:48.587 --> 01:02:49.620
You could've helped her!


01:02:49.771 --> 01:02:51.022
I didn't hear it.
This is your fault.


01:02:51.090 --> 01:02:53.841
Look, Otto... She's
dead. Janie is dead.


01:02:53.909 --> 01:02:56.244
I don't want to hear you trying
to rationalize this anymore.


01:02:59.981 --> 01:03:01.399
How are we going
to stop this thing?


01:03:14.979 --> 01:03:16.146
What are you doing here?


01:03:18.883 --> 01:03:20.283
When you came by
to see me earlier,


01:03:23.087 --> 01:03:24.754
part of me was excited


01:03:24.822 --> 01:03:26.456
that the mystery of opening up the
box was finally going to be over.


01:03:27.808 --> 01:03:29.309
Then I realized something.


01:03:31.477 --> 01:03:32.878
I was going to have
to see him again.


01:03:36.799 --> 01:03:38.067
Where is the box?


01:03:39.786 --> 01:03:42.171
If this was used to
trap that thing before,


01:03:42.238 --> 01:03:45.240
then we could use it
again somehow, correct?


01:03:45.308 --> 01:03:48.177
Only Duncan knows
how all this works.


01:03:49.880 --> 01:03:53.215
Against my better judgment, we're
going to have to pay him a visit.


01:03:53.283 --> 01:03:55.051
He started it.


01:03:55.117 --> 01:03:57.318
He's going to help us stop it.


01:04:03.693 --> 01:04:05.293
Shayla was here?


01:04:10.950 --> 01:04:12.500
(VIBRATING)


01:04:24.762 --> 01:04:25.829
Can you hear that?


01:04:25.897 --> 01:04:26.897
Uh-huh.


01:04:26.965 --> 01:04:27.965
Yeah?


01:04:29.367 --> 01:04:31.368
It's all yucky in there.


01:04:32.504 --> 01:04:33.470
Are you okay?


01:04:35.106 --> 01:04:37.073
Maybe you should
blow in it again.


01:04:37.141 --> 01:04:38.475
You know, just to make sure.


01:04:48.218 --> 01:04:50.085
Wanna check my ears now?


01:04:50.154 --> 01:04:51.154
(SOFT ROCK MUSIC PLAYING)


01:05:39.884 --> 01:05:41.217
(GROWLING)


01:05:55.283 --> 01:05:56.716
(SCREAMING)


01:06:06.326 --> 01:06:07.109
(EXCLAIMS)


01:06:17.154 --> 01:06:18.454
(GRUNTING)


01:06:25.229 --> 01:06:26.595
(SCREAMING)


01:06:45.714 --> 01:06:46.915
Kurtis?


01:07:32.126 --> 01:07:33.576
(SCREAMING)


01:07:49.058 --> 01:07:50.542
(SCREAMING)


01:07:55.765 --> 01:07:57.515
(SCREAMING)


01:08:03.907 --> 01:08:05.224
Shayla.


01:08:05.292 --> 01:08:06.808
Shayla. Shayla!


01:08:08.211 --> 01:08:11.028
It's okay. It's okay.


01:08:12.064 --> 01:08:13.331
It's okay.


01:08:15.500 --> 01:08:17.034
(SOBBING)


01:08:21.006 --> 01:08:22.490
Oh, my God.


01:08:22.557 --> 01:08:23.991
It was horrible.


01:08:25.961 --> 01:08:27.027
It was so real.


01:08:27.863 --> 01:08:29.129
It was so real.


01:08:30.983 --> 01:08:32.250
(SOBBING)


01:08:32.318 --> 01:08:33.651
Because it was real.


01:08:44.128 --> 01:08:45.411
Oh, Shayla.


01:08:45.479 --> 01:08:46.646
Shayla.


01:08:52.386 --> 01:08:53.620
Mom!


01:08:54.187 --> 01:08:55.071
Mom...


01:09:00.409 --> 01:09:02.277
Mom, what the hell is going on?


01:09:06.249 --> 01:09:07.650
What are you looking for?


01:09:11.054 --> 01:09:12.188
Leverage.


01:09:25.033 --> 01:09:27.468
The Bean Si was
persecuted like myself.


01:09:28.571 --> 01:09:30.271
It didn't have a choice.


01:09:32.057 --> 01:09:34.309
Its voice was silenced.


01:09:34.377 --> 01:09:36.077
Its cause, perverted.


01:09:38.497 --> 01:09:40.465
Common to royalty,


01:09:40.532 --> 01:09:42.700
hunted and pursued


01:09:42.767 --> 01:09:45.136
in an animalistic
pursuit of power.


01:09:46.722 --> 01:09:47.806
Its crime?


01:09:49.675 --> 01:09:52.026
To ask royalty to bow,


01:09:53.428 --> 01:09:55.462
to submit to its cry.


01:09:58.666 --> 01:10:01.551
That's what I've
been trying to say.


01:10:01.619 --> 01:10:04.204
The banshee screams because
it wants you to scream.


01:10:04.239 --> 01:10:06.857
That's why you can't give in
to it, give it what it wants.


01:10:06.925 --> 01:10:08.591
If you do that, it owns you.


01:10:10.995 --> 01:10:12.612
My tail is long,


01:10:13.881 --> 01:10:15.382
my coat is brown.


01:10:16.583 --> 01:10:17.834
I like the country,


01:10:19.235 --> 01:10:20.836
I like the town.


01:10:22.522 --> 01:10:24.273
I can live in a barn


01:10:24.942 --> 01:10:26.626
or live in a shed.


01:10:28.027 --> 01:10:31.097
And I come out to play
when you are in bed.


01:10:32.432 --> 01:10:34.233
My tail is long,


01:10:36.085 --> 01:10:37.620
my coat is brown.


01:10:39.573 --> 01:10:41.123
I like the country,


01:10:42.708 --> 01:10:43.875
I like the town.


01:10:45.110 --> 01:10:46.912
Or live in a shed.


01:10:48.581 --> 01:10:50.081
And I come out to play...


01:10:52.084 --> 01:10:53.050
Mom, look out!


01:10:53.936 --> 01:10:55.036
(TIRES SQUEALING)


01:10:58.357 --> 01:10:59.574
(GLASS SHATTERING)


01:11:06.265 --> 01:11:07.332
(GRUNTS)


01:11:15.440 --> 01:11:16.323
Kurtis.


01:11:18.643 --> 01:11:19.859
(SOBBING)


01:11:24.282 --> 01:11:25.799
We gotta get out.


01:11:25.867 --> 01:11:27.868
We gotta get out of the car.
Shayla, get out of the car!


01:11:34.074 --> 01:11:35.174
WHELAN: Get her out.


01:11:35.876 --> 01:11:37.026
Get her out!


01:11:42.933 --> 01:11:43.982
Get her away!


01:11:48.639 --> 01:11:49.772
Kurtis.


01:11:52.176 --> 01:11:53.526
(SCREAMING) Kurtis!
You gotta stay back.


01:11:53.594 --> 01:11:54.627
You can't do anything for him.


01:11:54.695 --> 01:11:55.962
SHAYLA: No...


01:11:56.881 --> 01:11:58.380
Otto, get the cross!


01:11:58.447 --> 01:12:00.648
Okay. Hold her.


01:12:00.683 --> 01:12:03.201
WHELAN: I'm here. I'm
here, Kurtis. I'm here.


01:12:03.352 --> 01:12:04.836
Keep Shayla safe.


01:12:06.405 --> 01:12:07.656
She's safe.


01:12:11.544 --> 01:12:13.211
It's okay. I'm here.


01:12:13.312 --> 01:12:14.662
Kurtis, I'm here, okay?


01:12:16.932 --> 01:12:17.765
WHELAN: It's okay.


01:12:18.467 --> 01:12:20.051
Kurtis. Kurtis!


01:12:24.306 --> 01:12:26.023
Professor, we got to
go. We gotta get out. Go.


01:12:26.091 --> 01:12:27.791
Go. Get the gun. Get the gun.


01:12:28.794 --> 01:12:29.827
Come on.


01:12:31.096 --> 01:12:31.879
(SHAYLA SOBBING)


01:12:31.947 --> 01:12:33.581
It's okay. It's okay. Let's go.


01:12:33.648 --> 01:12:35.583
It's okay. It's okay.


01:12:52.382 --> 01:12:53.216
(SCREECHING)


01:12:55.185 --> 01:12:57.270
(SCREAMING)


01:13:02.526 --> 01:13:04.594
Where are we going?
We are so dead.


01:13:04.662 --> 01:13:06.462
Mom, please. We
need to help him.


01:13:06.530 --> 01:13:08.314
This is crazy!


01:13:08.382 --> 01:13:09.632
Shut up!


01:13:09.700 --> 01:13:11.034
Doesn't anyone care?


01:13:11.101 --> 01:13:12.685
People are dying!


01:13:12.753 --> 01:13:15.372
I realize we're
dealing with crazy.


01:13:15.438 --> 01:13:17.306
But the only hope we have


01:13:17.374 --> 01:13:20.992
of stopping this nightmare is
with that professor up there.


01:13:21.060 --> 01:13:25.047
And if there's one chance of
saving my baby, I'm taking it.


01:13:27.183 --> 01:13:28.701
I say we keep walking.


01:13:31.554 --> 01:13:32.554
Fine.


01:13:33.106 --> 01:13:34.156
Whatever.


01:13:45.483 --> 01:13:46.551
WHELAN: Are you sure he's here?


01:13:47.118 --> 01:13:48.352
Yeah, he's here.


01:13:50.105 --> 01:13:51.205
(BUZZER BUZZING)


01:13:55.628 --> 01:13:57.128
Broderick, dear.


01:13:57.195 --> 01:13:58.695
It's Frederick.


01:13:58.763 --> 01:14:00.398
You know what this
is about. Open up.


01:14:02.467 --> 01:14:03.701
We know you're in there.


01:14:06.303 --> 01:14:08.388
My name is Professor
Moira Whelan


01:14:10.058 --> 01:14:11.475
and I've got something of yours.


01:14:21.135 --> 01:14:23.220
I'm sure you'd like
to know what was in it.


01:14:27.759 --> 01:14:29.159
(BUZZING)


01:14:31.978 --> 01:14:33.095
You're gonna need this.


01:14:37.283 --> 01:14:38.483
What is this place anyway?


01:14:39.719 --> 01:14:41.270
His home.


01:14:41.338 --> 01:14:43.388
But he likes to
call it Labbacalle.


01:15:36.941 --> 01:15:38.158
Open up, Broderick.


01:15:39.694 --> 01:15:41.812
(GUN FIRES)


01:15:41.879 --> 01:15:42.779
WHELAN: Get down.


01:15:44.381 --> 01:15:45.365
DUNCAN: Give me the cross.


01:15:46.216 --> 01:15:47.316
Give it to him!


01:15:47.383 --> 01:15:48.583
No!


01:15:48.651 --> 01:15:49.602
(GUN FIRES) He'll kill us.


01:15:51.638 --> 01:15:53.256
Who's shooting?


01:15:53.323 --> 01:15:54.423
Run!


01:15:56.009 --> 01:15:57.810
DUNCAN: Give me the cross!


01:15:57.878 --> 01:15:58.745
Get in!


01:16:01.231 --> 01:16:03.465
Oh, my God. This
guy is a lunatic!


01:16:03.533 --> 01:16:04.850
He's going to kill us.


01:16:16.078 --> 01:16:18.063
You really think that's going
to stop Old Man Crazy out there?


01:17:33.552 --> 01:17:35.420
(CELL PHONE RINGING)


01:18:14.810 --> 01:18:16.193
(BANSHEE SCREAMING)


01:18:20.581 --> 01:18:23.216
WHELAN: Now you've heard
the screams, you bastard.


01:18:23.283 --> 01:18:24.283
(GROANS)


01:19:29.131 --> 01:19:30.764
(WHIMPERING)


01:19:38.272 --> 01:19:39.873
(DOOR CLOSING)


01:20:30.422 --> 01:20:31.889
(SOBBING)


01:20:31.957 --> 01:20:33.274
Home run, princess.


01:20:36.996 --> 01:20:37.996
Come on out.


01:20:40.933 --> 01:20:42.867
I mean all of you.


01:20:42.935 --> 01:20:46.104
I will splatter princess'
brains all over the place.


01:20:51.876 --> 01:20:53.660
But I will negotiate.


01:20:57.565 --> 01:21:00.000
You must believe I was right, otherwise
you wouldn't be here, would you?


01:21:01.852 --> 01:21:03.570
I was right. Tell
me I was right.


01:21:03.637 --> 01:21:05.505
We're running out of time. I
know you can stop this thing.


01:21:05.573 --> 01:21:08.191
Say it. "You were right,
Duncan," and I'll consider it.


01:21:11.045 --> 01:21:12.012
Say it!


01:21:12.797 --> 01:21:13.897
You were right.


01:21:13.964 --> 01:21:15.048
That's it?


01:21:16.065 --> 01:21:17.283
And I'm sorry.


01:21:18.752 --> 01:21:19.752
Good.


01:21:21.671 --> 01:21:23.255
I can stop it.


01:21:23.323 --> 01:21:24.991
But I will do it my way.


01:21:32.149 --> 01:21:33.232
Okay.


01:21:33.901 --> 01:21:34.817
Long ago,


01:21:36.502 --> 01:21:37.820
a Templar Knight,


01:21:39.289 --> 01:21:41.657
a prince with royal Irish blood,


01:21:42.708 --> 01:21:46.311
devised a way to trap
a banshee's scream


01:21:46.379 --> 01:21:48.613
as a way to share
it with his enemies.


01:21:48.680 --> 01:21:50.114
(WHIRRING)


01:21:50.182 --> 01:21:51.600
(EXCLAIMS) Enemies?


01:21:53.569 --> 01:21:55.504
He martyred himself
to the curse.


01:21:58.123 --> 01:22:01.692
My main intent to
lead you to my box,


01:22:01.760 --> 01:22:03.678
not as revenge,


01:22:03.746 --> 01:22:06.181
I was sending a message.


01:22:06.248 --> 01:22:08.366
Your message has already
killed three people.


01:22:08.766 --> 01:22:09.866
Really?


01:22:10.451 --> 01:22:12.569
I hoped for more.


01:22:12.637 --> 01:22:14.605
(LAUGHS) But there's still time.


01:22:18.426 --> 01:22:20.310
What an exquisite design.


01:22:23.665 --> 01:22:25.316
But will it stop the banshee?


01:22:28.436 --> 01:22:29.536
Let's see.


01:22:31.623 --> 01:22:33.139
(SCREAMING)


01:22:34.558 --> 01:22:35.408
Run!


01:22:36.327 --> 01:22:37.326
Stop!


01:23:04.771 --> 01:23:07.638
So tell us how we trap
something that isn't real?


01:23:07.706 --> 01:23:08.874
Very carefully.


01:23:11.043 --> 01:23:14.546
Over there. We found that
when we found the box.


01:23:14.614 --> 01:23:16.180
DUNCAN: Very good, Freddie boy.


01:23:17.717 --> 01:23:18.884
Very good.


01:23:21.888 --> 01:23:23.255
That's what makes it flesh.


01:23:25.007 --> 01:23:26.007
Then let's go.


01:23:35.433 --> 01:23:36.818
(SCREAMS)


01:23:36.885 --> 01:23:38.085
(SOBBING) Kurtis.


01:23:40.672 --> 01:23:41.855
Kurtis.


01:23:48.328 --> 01:23:49.162
(SHAYLA SCREAMS)


01:23:49.230 --> 01:23:50.230
Wait. Shh.


01:23:52.666 --> 01:23:54.434
Sounds like it's
coming from below.


01:23:57.705 --> 01:23:58.972
The cave.


01:24:07.298 --> 01:24:08.398
I told you.


01:24:10.250 --> 01:24:11.751
I'll follow you anywhere you go.


01:24:12.486 --> 01:24:14.570
No! Get away.


01:24:15.671 --> 01:24:18.340
This isn't happening.
This isn't real.


01:24:29.536 --> 01:24:30.969
(ROARING)


01:24:36.209 --> 01:24:37.959
I know you want me to feel weak.


01:24:38.027 --> 01:24:41.146
You want me to feel old
and wretched like you.


01:24:41.213 --> 01:24:43.965
You want to drive me insane.


01:24:44.032 --> 01:24:47.418
But I won't let you take me.


01:24:47.485 --> 01:24:49.887
And I won't let you
get anyone else either.


01:24:55.427 --> 01:24:56.744
(SCREECHING)


01:24:58.697 --> 01:24:59.897
Shayla, don't move!


01:25:09.207 --> 01:25:12.192
Finally we meet face to face.


01:25:13.895 --> 01:25:15.913
(SCREECHING)


01:25:30.660 --> 01:25:32.044
Farewell, my lovely.


01:25:32.112 --> 01:25:33.228
(SCREAMING)


01:25:52.566 --> 01:25:54.066
That's enough out of you.


01:25:54.133 --> 01:25:55.066
Bitch.


01:26:05.845 --> 01:26:07.345
(SOBBING) You did it.


01:26:09.014 --> 01:26:10.147
Yes, we did.


01:26:10.215 --> 01:26:11.215
We did.


01:26:15.537 --> 01:26:17.138
Where's the box?


01:26:18.607 --> 01:26:20.491
What is it that you can keep


01:26:20.558 --> 01:26:22.942
after giving it to someone else?


01:26:31.553 --> 01:26:33.153
The answer is your word


01:26:33.220 --> 01:26:34.787
and your word means shit.

